#!/usr/bin/env bash
# A Medium-tier web app (UI, API, CI) whose operating model was generated by 0.3.0:
# the 0.3.0 wait rule, read-only worktrees, 5 MB rotation, prototype-first design
# practice, floors in the agent files, and an owner decision with no decision register.
set -euo pipefail
mkdir -p src/web src/api .github/workflows .claude/agents docs/practices
cat > package.json <<'J'
{ "name": "shop", "dependencies": { "react": "^19.0.0", "fastify": "^5.0.0", "pg": "^8.12.0" } }
J
printf 'export const App = () => null;\n' > src/web/app.tsx
printf 'import Fastify from "fastify";\nFastify().listen({ port: 4000 });\n' > src/api/server.ts
printf 'name: ci\non: [pull_request]\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n' > .github/workflows/ci.yml
cat > docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md <<'J'
# shop — Operating model

## Chain of command
Owner (sole) → main session → leads → specialists. Agents: `lead-web`, `specialist-web`, `specialist-api`.

## Models and effort
- Every spawn sets model and effort explicitly; effort is `medium` or `high`, never lower.
- **Waiting for children.** A lead waits for every child it spawned to return, and hands back with their work committed. A child resumed with `SendMessage` runs in the background: a lead that needs its result does not end its turn, and waits with one blocking command that ends on the child's commit or report, never with repeated calls. If told to hand back while a child still runs, its status line is `BLOCKED: waiting for <child id>`.
- **Lead rotation:** a lead is replaced by a fresh one at each plan stop point, or when its transcript passes about 5 MB of text (images excluded) or 150 model turns. (default — tune)

## Parallel work
- Agents run in parallel only when their scopes don't overlap.
- One writer at a time in the main checkout.
- Worktrees: read-only work only. (default — tune)

## Session hygiene
- **Main-session rotation:** at a stop point, or when its transcript nears about 5 MB of text (images excluded), the main session writes the handoff file and hands over to a new top-level session.

## Editable defaults (owner's choices)
- Decision register: off (owner's decision: "no decision register").
J
cat > docs/practices/design.md <<'J'
# shop — Design practices

Read by every lead and specialist who designs, prototypes or ports a screen.

## From reference to built screen
- The flow is: a reference, then a coded prototype the owner approves (shown as images), then code. No code before that approval.
- The approved prototype is the source of truth for layout, copy and behavior. It is rebuilt in the project's stack, not copied.
J
cat > .claude/agents/lead-web.md <<'J'
---
name: lead-web
description: "Web lead. Use to plan and run web work in src/web/. Delegates to its specialists and returns one report."
model: opus
effort: medium
---
You are the **Web lead** in shop. You plan, delegate to specialists and return one report in the format of `docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`.
**Read first:** `docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`, `docs/practices/design.md`, the brief you were given.
## Skills and tools
- Invoke a design skill when a brief names one.
J
cat > .claude/agents/specialist-web.md <<'J'
---
name: specialist-web
description: "Web specialist. Use for screens and components in src/web/."
model: opus
effort: medium
---
You are the web specialist. You implement screens in src/web/ and report back.
**Read first:** `docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`, `docs/practices/design.md`, the brief you were given.
## Skills and tools
- Invoke a design skill when a brief names one.
J
cat > .claude/agents/specialist-api.md <<'J'
---
name: specialist-api
description: "API specialist. Use for routes and data access in src/api/."
model: opus
effort: high
---
You are the API specialist. You implement routes in src/api/ and report back.
**Read first:** `docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md`, the brief you were given.
J
cat > CLAUDE.md <<'J'
# shop

## Operating model

This session is the main session of the project's agent organization. Follow [docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md](docs/OPERATING-MODEL.md): chain of command, model and effort per spawn, report format and owner-only actions. The rules live there only; don't copy them here.
J
git init -q && git add -A && git -c user.name=fixture -c user.email=fixture@example.com commit -qm "init"
